  "caption": "Quinn walked 25,000 steps a day in new shoes on holiday. By day three the arch was on strike, and Dr Google said plantar fasciitis.\n\nArch pain isn't always plantar fasciitis. Tendons, midfoot joints, bone stress and nerves can all be involved, and a sudden jump in walking load or a footwear change often comes first.\n\nWhat often helps: ease the load that set it off, do regular heel raises for calf and foot strength, review your shoes (insoles or taping can support the painful phase), and return to walking or running gradually. Arch pain often settles in 6–12 weeks with a good plan.\n\nOne sore spot that's worse with impact, tingling or burning, or a foot changing shape is worth getting checked.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
